60,3,1,talk,May,,I'm leaning toward Option D. We tried something similar years ago and it actually worked! Why ignore it?,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option D is a fantasy. We have no one left in the late-turn pool to actually drive the trains.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I think Option B might help with the mid-city delays, but Option C could fix the connection times.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option C sounds lovely, but those pre-war shells are so unpredictable. I worry it will stall.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option A is the only one that addresses the contractor fees. We cannot keep paying three different companies.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're such a killjoy! We can just hire more people. Let's go with the one that works.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Hiring is a process, May, not a magic spell. Option A is logical, though it doesn't solve the staffing crisis.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, would Option A actually make the trips faster, or just the payment easier?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I think it would make the journey smoother. But @Jonathan, will the ferry operators agree to it?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, it won't make the bus faster, but it stops the money from leaking out to contractors.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,I still think we're ignoring the evidence. Option D is a proven winner if we just look back.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Proven winners are useless if the players are too tired to take the field. I'll support Option A.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,I'm worried about the time loss. Option C fixes the bottlenecks where people actually lose minutes.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am afraid Option C will be a nightmare of hidden voids. I think Option A is the safest path.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,Option A is the only one that stops the budget from being a series of arguments over contractor pots.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,"Fine, fine! If you all want to be boring and safe, I'll see where the wind blows.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Safety is often mistaken for boredom by those who don't have to manage the fallout.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I still feel Option C is the most helpful for the passengers, but I see the budget concerns.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,Let us choose the path that brings us the most peace and the least amount of unexpected trouble.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I believe we have reached a consensus on the most sustainable choice.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
